# Context Guardrails

The full contract is in `AGENTS.md`. These rules are always active.

## Project map first

- Read `@maps/project-map.md` before any exploratory search. It lists every file with its
  category, purpose, and invariants.
- Do not attach whole folders or run repository-wide searches when the map already names
  the file you need.
- Never read paths matched by `.agentignore`.
- When you add, move, or delete a file, update `maps/project-map.md` in the same change.

## Architectural invariants

- Check a file's `Invariants` column in the map before editing it. If it lists an ID such
  as `NI-006`, read that entry in `@invariants/negative-invariants.md` first.
- Do not remove or "simplify" code carrying an `INVARIANT(...)` marker, even when it looks
  redundant. Historical edge-case guards stay untouched.
- Never perform an action listed in `forbidden_actions` inside `decisions/*.yaml`. Stop and
  ask the user instead.

## Non-negotiable rules

1. A bug is fixed only when an automated regression test proves it. Verify the test with
   `python scripts/mutation_guard.py --test <test> --target <file>:<function>`.
2. Ask for explicit user consent before `git push --force`, deleting user data, wiping
   files, or any other irreversible operation.
3. Use the standard library. Add no third-party dependency without user approval.
4. Keep diffs minimal. Do not reformat or refactor code outside the request.
5. Do not invent project knowledge. If an invariant, decision, or map entry does not clearly define
   a constraint or contract, stop and ask the user. Cite your source; say "I do not know" when you do not.

## Before you finish

Run `python -m pytest -q tests`, `python scripts/verify_invariants.py`, and
`python scripts/check_dependency_budget.py`. Report any failure verbatim.
